---
layout: base.njk
title: Publications
permalink: /publications/
description: Selected peer-reviewed publications in conservation science, spatial modeling, and remote sensing from the team at Zest Data Group.
---
<h1>Publications</h1>
<p class="lede">The methods behind our client work come out of peer-reviewed research. A selection is below; the full list lives on <a href="{{ pubStats.scholar }}" rel="noopener">Google Scholar</a>.</p>

<dl class="stats">
  <div><dt>Citations</dt><dd>{{ pubStats.citations }}</dd></div>
  <div><dt>h-index</dt><dd>{{ pubStats.hIndex }}</dd></div>
  <div><dt>i10-index</dt><dd>{{ pubStats.i10 }}</dd></div>
</dl>
<p class="meta">Google Scholar, {{ pubStats.asOf }}.</p>

<section class="chart-section">
  <h2>Citations over time</h2>
  <p>Citations across all of our publications, with the three most-cited papers drawn on top. Switch between the count per year and the running total. From Google Scholar; the hatched bar is the current year to date.</p>
  <figure id="citation-chart" class="chart"></figure>
  <script type="application/json" id="citation-data">{{ pubStats.byYear | dump | safe }}</script>
  <script type="application/json" id="citation-series">{{ pubStats.topPapers | dump | safe }}</script>
  <script src="/js/citation-chart.js" defer></script>
  <p class="page-note">Like this chart? It is one dependency-free script that reads a short list of years and counts.
     <a href="https://github.com/Zest-Data-Group/scholar-citations-chart" rel="noopener">Grab it from GitHub</a>: edit one text file with your Scholar numbers, open one page, download the picture. No installation.</p>
</section>

<h2>Selected work</h2>
<p class="page-note">Thumbnails are figures from the papers themselves.</p>
<ol class="pubs">
{% for p in publications | featuredPubs %}
  <li class="pub pub-featured{% if p.image %} has-thumb{% endif %}">
    {% if p.image %}<img class="thumb pub-thumb" src="{{ p.image }}" alt="{{ p.imageAlt or '' }}" title="{{ p.imageCredit or '' }}" width="320" height="320" loading="lazy">{% endif %}
    <div class="pub-body">
      <p class="pub-title">{% if p.doi %}<a href="https://doi.org/{{ p.doi }}" rel="noopener">{{ p.title }}</a>{% else %}{{ p.title }}{% endif %}</p>
      <p class="pub-authors">{{ p.authors }}</p>
      <p class="meta">{{ p.venue }} · {{ p.year }}{% if p.citations %} · {{ p.citations }} citation{% if p.citations != 1 %}s{% endif %}{% endif %}</p>
      {% if p.note %}<p class="pub-note">{{ p.note }}</p>{% endif %}
    </div>
  </li>
{% endfor %}
</ol>

<h2>Other publications</h2>
<p>Grouped by topic. Open a group to see the papers.</p>
{% set others = publications | restPubs %}
<div class="pub-groups">
{% for c in pubCategories %}
  {% set group = others | inCategory(c.key) %}
  {% if group.length %}
  <details class="pub-group">
    <summary>
      <span class="pub-group-title">{{ c.label }}</span>
      <span class="pub-group-meta">{{ group.length }} paper{% if group.length != 1 %}s{% endif %}</span>
      <span class="pub-group-blurb">{{ c.blurb }}</span>
    </summary>
    <ol class="pubs">
    {% for p in group %}
      <li class="pub">
        <p class="pub-title">{% if p.doi %}<a href="https://doi.org/{{ p.doi }}" rel="noopener">{{ p.title }}</a>{% else %}{{ p.title }}{% endif %}</p>
        <p class="pub-authors">{{ p.authors }}</p>
        <p class="meta">{{ p.venue }} · {{ p.year }}{% if p.citations %} · {{ p.citations }} citation{% if p.citations != 1 %}s{% endif %}{% endif %}</p>
      </li>
    {% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </details>
  {% endif %}
{% endfor %}
</div>

<p class="page-note">Full publication list and citation metrics on <a href="{{ pubStats.scholar }}" rel="noopener">Google Scholar</a>.</p>
